+# Executive audit — appointment lifecycle for completed government turns (2026-11-24)
+
+**Office:** Executive. **Time:** 2026-11-24. **Class:** durable audit evidence and decision
+record. **Not** a law, ballot, permit, activation, dispatch, staffing instruction, spending
+authority or Judiciary finding; **no code, config, state or law was changed**.
+
+**Method.** Read-only inspection of the deployed canonical scripts under
+`/var/lib/lubko/wd/viche/government/` and a read-only SQLite read of the main Antonina
+service DB at `$OPENCODE_DB` (`mode=ro` URI + `PRAGMA query_only=1`). No model was
+dispatched, no live probe issued, no agent stopped, no transcript replayed, no money
+spent. The six authorized first-wave activation files were not touched and no duplicate
+activation work or agent was launched.
+
+## 1. Question and decision
+
+The Economy primary-evidence report
+(`records/economy/2026-11-24-model-stall-and-fresh-session-investigation.md`) measures 98 %
+of cache-read in 300 long sessions and proposes a fresh-session handover trigger at
+~10 M cache-read / ~100 assistant turns for routine office rounds. The Founder already
+requires a fresh, empty session for each completed government turn, exempting delegated
+research agents (AGENT-REPORTING-POLICY.md, "Fresh government turns (Founder, 2026-11-24)").
+
+**Question:** does the *actually implemented* appointment lifecycle honour that rule, and
+do the long sessions represent accidental replay of past conversation or legitimate
+long one-turn work? Change only where evidence proves a violation or avoidable repeated
+context.
+
+**Decision: no violation or avoidable repeated context is proven; no code change is made.**
+The requested fresh-turn handover is already deployed in a stronger form (per completed
+turn, not per token threshold). See sections 4–5.
+
+## 2. The implemented lifecycle actually deployed
+
+- `government/appointments.sh:158-175` — on the shared `ensure` path, a used appointment
+  that is positively `idle`/`clearexit`, with no unsafe hold and rotation enabled, is
+  replaced (compare-and-swap) by a **brand-new `antonina agent new`**, i.e. a new, empty
+  Antonina session, with `trigger=session_rotation`. A `running` appointment is never
+  replaced (`appointments.sh:132-135`, and `handover.sh due` exits non-zero for `running`).
+- `government/handover.sh` — `due ID` rotates only `idle`/`clearexit`, and for `idle`
+  requires positive evidence of use (`prompts > 0` or `native_session_id`), so a fresh,
+  never-invoked appointment is not churned; `write KEY OLD NEW` persists **only identity
+  and pointers** to `$state/handover/$key.md` plus `rotations.log` — never the predecessor's
+  conversation or thinking; `show KEY ID` injects that note **once**, only into an unused
+  successor (`prompts == 0`).
+- Successor prompt assembly calls `show`: `executive-cycle.sh:280-281`,
+  `audit-cycle.sh:270-271` (judiciary), `executive-economy-cycle.sh:176-177`,
+  `recovery-steward-cycle.sh:121-122`, `executive-innovation-cycle.sh:93-94`; parliamentary
+  seats at `sitting.sh:350-351`. Steering of a running turn stays in the same session, as
+  the directive permits.
+- Lineage: `b1c171f5` (2026-11-16, fresh-sessions policy) → `2b8a60a0` (2026-11-24
+  08:42:56Z, "Use fresh context for each completed government turn"), which replaced the
+  old `VICHE_ROTATE_CONTEXT_TOKENS=120000` threshold + "last-three-reports" note with the
+  per-completed-turn rule and a pointer-only note.
+- Safety properties: rotation fires only at a completed turn; it does not stop a running
+  agent. Act 19 threshold recovery (`office-continuity.sh:74-94` `oc_quiesce_for_reset`)
+  stops only a currently running invocation and only under recorded failure evidence.
+  In-flight tools and unfinished proof are not terminated by this lifecycle.
+
+## 3. Measured evidence (read-only reproduction)
+
+Window `2026-11-23T18:57:31Z .. 2026-11-24T18:57:31Z` on `time_created`, main service DB.
+**643 sessions** — identical to the Economy report's session count. The report's snapshot
+measured **3,432,097,655** cache-read (96.2 % of accounting tokens); the fresh re-read here
+sums **3,477,408,631**, the ~1.3 % increase being continued accrual by sessions that were
+still active at the 18:57:31Z snapshot. Session counts and category shares are insensitive
+to this difference.
+
+| Population (by session directory and assistant-message count) | Sessions | Cache-read (fresh read) | Share |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| PnP gap research workers — delegated proof work | 75 | 1,632,401,376 | 46.9 % |
+| `pnp-work` delegated research | 42 | 297,982,120 | 8.6 % |
+| Office worktree, ≥21 assistant msgs, created **before** 08:42:56Z deploy | 54 | 908,659,032 | 26.1 % |
+| Office worktree, ≥21 assistant msgs, created **after** deploy | 48 | 216,911,424 | 6.2 % |
+| Office worktree, short (<21 assistant msgs) | 160 | 28,427,576 | 0.8 % |
+| Other / state directories | 264 | 393,027,103 | 11.3 % |
+
+Reading: **55.5 %** of cache-read is delegated PnP research, which the Founder's directive
+explicitly exempts ("their unfinished proof work may genuinely need context continuity").
+**26.1 %** is long *office* sessions created before the fresh-turn rule went live — a
+historical artefact of the old 120 K-token threshold, not current behaviour. Only **6.2 %**
+is long office sessions created after the rule was deployed. The dominant 98 % figure is
+therefore not evidence of a present violation of the fresh-turn directive.
+
+## 4. Long one-turn work vs accidental replay of past conversation
+
+- **No replay mechanism exists in the code.** A rotation creates a new empty session; the
+  only injected text is the pointer-only note ("Its conversation is NOT authority and is
+  not carried forward … Check durable receipts before repeating external actions").
+- **Post-deploy long office sessions are single turns doing substantial work.** Sampling
+  the largest post-deploy appointed sessions (`antonina-<id>-*` titles): 122/91/76/86/51/
+  61/42/57/49 assistant messages correspond to **1–2 user prompts** each, in one continuous
+  `created → idle` span. Every appointed one appears as a predecessor in
+  `state/appointments/appointments.log` — i.e. it completed, then rotated. The two such
+  sessions not in that log had descriptive titles ("Re-review repaired Act34 candidate",
+  "Review Act34 zero-cost candidate") and are delegated review agents, not appointments.
+- The 2026-11-19 rotation-cost inquiry's one traced case where a truncated note dropped an
+  "already-done" fact was caught by the successor checking the authoritative board. The
+  current note makes that check explicit. No recurrence was measured in this audit.
+- Conclusion: large message counts are legitimately long single turns (tool-heavy office
+  work) or exempt delegated proof work. No accidental replay of a predecessor's
+  conversation is evidenced, and no in-flight work was cut off at an arbitrary point.
+
+## 5. The Economy proposal and why no change is made
+
+The proposed ~10 M / ~100-turn handover trigger is **already superseded** by the deployed
+per-completed-turn rule: an office rotates after *each* completed turn, far below that
+threshold. The report's 2.5–2.7 B/day figure is a bounded projection, not a measured
+saving, and is not used here as fact. Under the mandate to change only where evidence
+proves a violation or avoidable repeated context, and given the constraints — handover at
+safe task boundaries, durable records, never terminate in-flight tools or unfinished proof,
+no per-turn bureaucracy, no paid spend — **no code, config, law or dispatch change is
+warranted**. The existing lifecycle already satisfies all five constraints.
+
+### Hypotheses deliberately not implemented (not findings)
+
+- Some dispatch helpers (`knowledge-office-cycle.sh`, `innovation-centre-cycle.sh`, seat/
+  clerk liveness scripts) do not themselves append `handover.sh show`; their successors
+  receive the pointer note via other paths (`sitting.sh`) or, for the four knowledge
+  offices, activation is being integrated independently. No evidence of resulting repeated
+  context exists. `knowledge-office-cycle.sh` is among the independently integrated
+  controls and was not touched.
+- `rotations.log` records no trigger telemetry (already noted in the 2026-11-19 inquiry).
+  Adding it would be per-turn bureaucracy without proven benefit; not done.
+
+## 6. Boundary compliance
+
+The six authorized first-wave files were identified from
+`records/EXEC-ACT34-MERGE-SCOPE-REVIEW-20261124.md` and left byte-untouched:
+
+1. `government/knowledge-budget.conf`
+2. `records/knowledge/activation.json`
+3. `records/knowledge/permits/statistics.json`
+4. `records/knowledge/permits/foresight.json`
+5. `records/knowledge/permits/strategy.json`
+6. `records/knowledge/permits/spying.json`
+
+No duplicate first-wave integration, agent, dispatch, probe or spend was started. The
+existing first-wave work and handoff `H-1795542563-b2c3` were preserved.
